    logger that silently converts a crash into a log line is worse than no logger.

  [1mHonest note on the Node side:[0m [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m is a hello-world. Beyond [38;5;153mapp.start[39m and the uncaught handlers there's
  nothing there worth instrumenting. I'm not going to invent events for it.

  [1mTesting.[0m The logger is pure enough to test properly, and the highest-value test in the whole change is the one
  asserting a password never reaches a sink — that's the failure mode with real consequences. I'd cover: denylist
  matching (including nested objects and substring keys like [38;5;153mnewPassword[39m), non-object [38;5;153mdata[39m rejection, 200-char
  truncation, username truncation, level thresholds, buffer bounded at 50, and the buffer-captures-below-threshold
  behavior. [38;5;153mnode:test[39m is built in, so this stays zero-dependency.

  The repo has no tooling configured at all — no scripts, no linter, no test runner. It's cheapest to decide that now:

